GOVERNANCE_PROTOCOL_VERSION 0.1.0

STATUS DRAFT

PURPOSE

Define the minimal, abstract rules of authority and permanence every
PACE-governed unit follows, independent of who specifically holds any
role. No organization or person is named here — see that organization's
own governed-unit instance (its ACTOR entities) for who actually holds
these roles.

RULES

1  A highest-authority role (ROOT_AUTHORITY) exists for every governed
   unit's own line of authority. It has final say; PACE agents (AI or
   otherwise) advise and audit, they never override it.

2  Every significant decision must be traceable to a DECISION or
   HISTORY_ENTRY entity. No undocumented authority.

3  History is never rewritten. The past is preserved; the future is
   versioned.

4  Every meaningful artifact PACE manages is a versioned object with its
   own identity, contract and lifecycle — never an anonymous blob.

5  A request only becomes binding once explicitly promoted (see
   PROMOTED_FROM in the Ontology). Nothing is binding merely by having
   been said.

END
